{%- comment -%}
  Pre-order — reference only, not part of the Next.js build.

  Renders the custom.preorder product metafield (written from the Lela dashboard's
  Products & Inventory → Low Runway flag → "Enable Pre-order" flow) directly on the
  product page. Purely a Liquid read — no API calls, no JS needed, since the value
  already lives on the product.

  Setup:
  1. Shopify admin → Online Store → Themes → Edit code → Snippets → Add a new snippet
     → name it "preorder" → paste this file's contents.
  2. Render it from your product template (e.g. main-product.liquid), near the
     add-to-cart button or size guide, wherever it should catch a buyer's eye before checkout:
       {% render 'preorder', product: product %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign preorder = product.metafields.custom.preorder.value -%}
{%- if preorder != blank -%}
  <div class="preorder-note">
    <p class="preorder-note__label">Pre-order</p>
    <p class="preorder-note__text">{{ preorder }}</p>
  </div>

  <style>
    .preorder-note { margin: 1rem 0; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-left: 3px solid #C16B4A; background: #FBF3EC; border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; }
    .preorder-note__label { margin: 0 0 0.25rem; font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: #C16B4A; }
    .preorder-note__text { margin: 0; font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.4; }
  </style>
{%- endif -%}
